Problem: Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters (LC 3)

Pattern: Variable Size Sliding Window + Hash Set

Approach:

Use two pointers:
left → start of the window.
right → end of the window.
Use an unordered_set to store the characters in the current window.
For each right:
While the current character already exists in the set:
Remove s[left] from the set.
Increment left.
Insert s[right] into the set.

Update the maximum window length using:

maxLen = max(maxLen, right - left + 1);
Return maxLen.

Time Complexity: O(n)

Space Complexity: O(min(n, 128)) (or O(min(n, alphabet size)))